{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It holds the same keys and answers the same queries as "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", with the same names, but has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a vertex per key and per branching point rather than per symbol: O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") vertices for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" keys,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"however long they are. That suits keys with long shared prefixes, such as file paths or URLs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Lookup, insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"d","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"σ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for a key of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols that passes "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"d"}]},{"type":"text","text":" vertices of at most "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"σ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" children."}]},{"code":["let paths = RadixTree([\"\/usr\/bin\", \"\/usr\/lib\", \"\/usr\/local\/bin\"])","paths.contains(\"\/usr\/lib\")                                   \/\/ true","paths.elements(withPrefix: \"\/usr\/l\").map { String($0) }      \/\/ [\"\/usr\/lib\", \"\/usr\/local\/bin\"]","paths.longestPrefix(of: \"\/usr\/bin\/swift\").map { String($0) } \/\/ \"\/usr\/bin\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" links, and the edge labels are slices of one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffer of symbols, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 vertices and label symbols, and copying","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/PrefixView"]},{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/init()","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/init(_: